### Final_keyword
-- cannot ber override by child class.
-- the final keyword is used to declare something that cannot be change. it can be used with:-
     Variables
     Methods
     Classes 
** final keyword important
- prevent mistake-- like pi = 3.14 if we make the final no one can change it later by mistake
- protect importent code

**  CODE
final class Parent {
    final int x = 10;
    final void show() {
        System.out.println("Final method in Parent");
        System.out.println("Final variable x = " + x);
    }
}
class Child {   // cannot extend Parent
    void test() {
        System.out.println("Child class");
    }
}
public class FinalKeywordDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Parent obj = new Parent();
        obj.show();
        // obj.x = 20;   // ❌ Compile-time error (final variable)
    }
}
